    {
      "chapter": "Print layout and assembly order",
      "duration_ms": 1800,
      "note": "The screw prints on its through-axis flat. Stand the nut on its end, and put the jaw and keeper on their broad end faces. Five separated parts fit within 204 by 166 mm, including the conservative 235.5 by 256 mm dual-tool bed. Insert the nut, turn in the screw, slide on the jaw and install the keeper. Keep supports off for the first fit experiment; inspect the short housing bore bridges before loading."
